{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice","id":1404465,"title":"Mastery through Artifice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-24T15:38:09-07:00","id":1404465,"title":"Mastery through Artifice","content":"In another thread I proposed a possible means for some Exalts to access the Mastery Keyword through the use of a Heathstone (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404345-master-s-stone\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...master-s-stone</a>). The more I think about it though, the less convinced I am that it is the right way to go.<br /> <br /> However I do remember that there was an Artifact back in 1st or 2nd Ed that enhanced an Exalt's use of Martial Arts... and I am trying to remember what it was and if it might be possible to rework the idea to serve this purpose. Sadly I don't have access to my 1st and 2nd Ed books at this time and can remember neither the name nor the book it was located in (I would like to say Oadenol's Codex or Wonders of the Lost Age (Books of Sorcery: Volume 1 and 3)... but I am unsure of either. If I remember correctly, they appeared as inscribed bracers that described martial art forms. I want to say they were called Kata Bracers or something along those lines... but I simply don't recall them well enough to be sure.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly they were often made with traces of Starmetal and enhanced the use of Martial Art Charms in some way. I think this is likely the best way to achieve the affect I am after, namely allowing non-Solar and non-Sidereal martial artists to access the effects of the Mastery Keyword on Charms. That said, I an not entirely sure how powerful an Artifact this originally was or should be for 3rd Edition.<br /> <br /> Given that there are no hard rules as to what a given level of Artifacts can innately achieve (there really is no difference in the mundane applications between a 3 dot Daiklave and a 5 dot Daiklave), I have looked at the kinds of evocations that can be produced by the various levels. 3 dot Artifacts allow one to learn evocations that would be roughly equivalent to what they would normally be able to produce with an equivalent skill level. 4 dot Artifacts however allow for more potent effects than would normally be available to an Exalt of equivalent skill level, allowing for a unique playstyle for the owner. I would see accessing the Mastery Keyword as being soundly within the 4 dot range of ability... as the effects that Mastery produces tends to make a Martial Art charm more potent than what is normally possible for an Exalt and allows a very unique playstyle that would not normally be available to many Exalts.I do not see this as being the same as the almost overwhelming might that a 5 dot Artifact often provides, thus I am fairly certain that a 4 dot Artifact would be sufficient for this effect... powerful, but not overtly game changing (any more so than a Solar or Sidereal having access to these effects naturally is).<br /> <br /> If anyone can tell me the name of the original Artifact I am thinking of and where to locate its write-up (or provide a rough description of it), I might be able to refine this idea better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T00:25:04-07:00","id":1404535,"title":"","content":"Perfected Kata Bracers are in Oadenol's Codex. I can't recall which, if any, book they were in in 1E.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> PERFECTED KATA BRACERS - 4 dots<br /> <br /> Perfected kata bracers are prayer strips crafted of a single magical material and curled into bracers. <br /> <br /> The strips\u2019 sutras are starmetal engravings, except in starmetal bracers\u2014they use orichalcum. <br /> <br /> Attunement costs eight motes. When the character activates a Form-type Charm, the sutras inscribed on the bracers glow and lift from the artifact to engulf the character in light for a brief moment. For the rest of the scene, she gains several benefits.<br /> <br /> She adds her Essence to the accuracy, damage and defense of her unarmed attacks and of attacks made with the active Form-type Charm\u2019s particular weapons. She may choose to inflict bashing or lethal damage at will and she may parry lethal attacks unarmed. In addition:<br /> <br /> Orichalcum bracers let Solars inflict aggravated damage on creatures of darkness.<br /> <br /> Moonsilver bracers provide Lunars additional flexibility, so they ignore cover and shields.<br /> <br /> Jade bracers add Essence to Dragon-Blooded\u2019s soak and 2 to the Rate of their attacks.<br /> <br /> Starmetal eases the flow of martial Essence for Sidereals, reducing the cost of activating Charms of the same style by two motes (minimum 1).<br /> <br /> Soulsteel makes an Abyssal\u2019s attack fatal if it inflicts more levels of damage than a mortal victim\u2019s Stamina.<br /> <br /> Perfected kata bracers provide very significant effects. A skilled martial artist wielding them in battle has a significant advantage over her opponents, especially when wielding artifact martial-arts weapons. They suffer the small drawback of being incredibly obvious. If their benefits weren\u2019t limited to the battlefield, the bracers might be Artifact 5.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> My 3E homebrew suggestion would be something like this:<br /> <br /> Perfected Kata Bracers - 4 dots<br /> <br /> Perfected kata bracers are prayer strips crafted of orichalcum and curled into bracers. Their sutras are engraved in starmetal.<br /> <br /> When the character activates a Form-type Charm, the sutras inscribed on the bracers glow and lift from the artifact to engulf the character in golden light, equivalent to a Burning Anima, for the duration of the Form-type Charm. Whilst so engulfed the character may choose to inflict bashing or lethal damage at will and she may parry lethal and ranged attacks unarmed. <br /> <br /> Characters who are Resonant with either Orichalcum or Starmetal are Resonant with Perfected Kata Bracers (even if they are Dissonant with the other material). Characters who are not Resonant with either material are Neutral, unless they are Dissonant with one or the other material, in which case they are Dissonant. Solars and Sidereals are always Resonant with Perfected Kata Bracers, regardless of other effects. <br /> <br /> Perfected Kata Bracers cost 3m to attune allow the awakening of the following Evocations:<br /> <br /> Tiger-And-Bear Unity<br /> Preqs: Essence 2, one Form type Charm<br /> Cost: - (+5m)<br /> Type: Permenant, Resonant<br /> <br /> On activating a Form-type Charm, the user may spend an additional 5m to ignore the Terrestrial keyword for Charms in that style for as long as the Form remains active.<br /> <br /> Resonant: Ignore this Evocation's minimum Essence requirement. <br /> <br /> Reach-Heaven-Through-Violence<br /> Preqs: Essence 2, one Form type Charm<br /> Cost: - (+5m, 1WP)<br /> Type: Permenant, Resonant<br /> <br /> On activating a Form-type Charm, the user may spend an additional 5m 1WP to activate this Evocation. So long as the user is not limited by the Terrestrial keyword for Charms of this style, they may activate that style's Mastery effects as long as they remain in Form.<br /> <br /> Resonant: Ignore this Evocation's minimum Essence requirement. <br /> <br /> Golden Monkey Enlightenment <br /> Prereqs: Essence 3, one Evocation this Charm enhances<br /> Cost: - (+1WP)<br /> Type: Permenant, Resonant<br /> <br /> When activating Tiger-And-Bear Unity or Reach-Heaven-Through-Violence the user may send an additional +1WP to activate Golden Monkey Enlightenment, those Evocations extend their benefits to all Martial Arts Charms the user knows, not just those of the Form's style.<br /> <br /> Resonant: This Evocation unlocks automatically for free once its prerequisites are met. <br /> <br /> Shining Strike<br /> Prereqs: Essence 1<br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Uniform, Mastery, Dissonant, Resonant<br /> <br /> Whilst engulfed in the bracer's golden light, the user may pay 3m to add a single success to a Martial Arts attack or raise their Martial Arts based Parry by one. If the Martial Arts Attack is placed in a Flurry, reduce the Flurry penalty to -1 (for the Attack only).<br /> <br /> This Evocation unlocks automatically for free the first time the wielder uses a Form-type Charm whilst attuned to the Bracers.<br /> <br /> Mastery: If the user has access to Mastery of the Martial Art being used, add two successes or raise Parry by two instead. The user's Decisive attacks also deal Aggravated damage to Creatures of Darkness and Mortals.<br /> <br /> Dissonant: This Evocation does not automatically unlock and must be purchased as normal.<br /> <br /> Resonant: The wielder always uses the Mastery effects of this Evocation, even if they do not have Mastery of the Martial Art being used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-26-2020, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T00:30:05-07:00","id":1404537,"title":"","content":"Once again, Jade is the best magical material in 2e. Maybe Starmetal beating it out ever so slightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T01:44:22-07:00","id":1404545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404537#post1404537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, Jade is the best magical material in 2e. Maybe Starmetal beating it out ever so slightly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rate sucks.<br /> <br /> Punch had Rate 3, Kick Rate 2 and Clinch Rate 1. So without bracers you could already make 6 attacks with -7 Accuracy scaling up to -12. Ok, +2 Rate could give you 12 attacks... but you're rolling -13 to -24 dice. That's not helpful. Rate didn't apply to Charm Flurries and eventually was capped at 5.<br /> <br /> Essence to Soak is pretty boss, but the Starmetal discount is WAAAY better.<br /> <br /> Hearthstone Bracers and Weapons, Jade is easily best. Even with Speed Limit (although speed limit means you want Jade bracers and a weapon of something else). Armor? Jade is a solid option but it's not clear cut (again, I favor Starmetal). Magitech -- Jade sucks.<br /> <br /> Jade is a lot better than Moonsilver and Adamant. But it was only ever on par with Starmetal and Orichalcum. (Soulsteal was either awesome or sucked depending how much the writers hated Abyssals.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-25-2020, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T15:12:39-07:00","id":1404650,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> Thanks for the information on the 2nd Ed Perfected Kata Bracers.<br /> <br /> As for your take on them for 3rd Ed... it is a little lack-luster in my opinion.<br /> <br /> The two Exalts that are normally resonant with this artifact to get the benefit of 3 of the 4 Evocations (in other words don't need to wait until Essence 2+ to learn them) have no need for those Evocations as they naturally have access to the Mastery Keyword and are not subject to the Terrestrial Keyword.<br /> <br /> As for the last of the 4 Evocations, the one that is automatically learned, again, the Solars and Sidereal have more efficient means of gaining a success or raising their Parry than a 3 mote cost effect. In short... this artifact does not live up to a 4 dot cost for these Exalts... in providing a game-play style change for the character by unlocking effects that they couldn't do on their own. Even the Mastery effect of doubling what the normal Evocation provides and doing Aggravated damage is less than impressive for the costs to get.<br /> <br /> As for other Exalts, it is rather over-punishing for little real gain. Only one type of Exalt really needs the Evocation that allows one to ignore the effects of the Terrestrial Keyword... Dragon-Bloods. Beyond that, you have rather steep costs for the three Evocations +5 motes and 1 or 2 Willpower, thus a Dragon-Blooded will be spending a significant portion of their Essence Pool (10 motes) and force of will (1 or 2 Willpower) just to access the relatively minor gains that Mastery provides... and only so long as they are able to remain under the effects of a Form Charm. This is in addition to the fact that they need 2+ Essence just to learn those Evocations.<br /> <br /> Yes, a standard starting Terrestrial will start with Essence 2 (while other Exalts do not), but this means that they will have to give up 2 of their starting charms to learn the basic Evocations... in addition to however many charms it would cost them to learn a Martial Art to the Form Charm (assuming they have the Essence rating to reach the Form Charm). For those who start off at Essence 1 (young Dragon-Bloods and most other Exalts by default)... having to wait until Essence 2 can sometimes be a fair wait. Added to the relative uselessness of the Artifact in the hands of the two Exalts that would have the easiest time using it... and it just seems a little sloppy in design that doesn't live up to its potential. It really puts a lot of hurdles that have to be overcome so that most Exalts have to pay prohibitive amounts to access fairly minor effects (in respect to the cost paid). It honestly looks like it is designed more to punish a player than to reward them with a new style of play.<br /> <br /> I may be overly harsh in my analysis... but it really does seem to be a lot of effort to pay a significant amount for such a small effect... not what most people likely expect when they purchase a 4 dot artifact. That said, I do see potential in the principles and I understand the reasoning behind the choices... but I find the execution of the design to be a little sloppy and overly punishing for little real gain. It really doesn't measure up to the effects that other 4 dot artifacts grant their owners, even when taking into account they Exalt type using it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T19:08:04-07:00","id":1404689,"title":"","content":"<i><b><u>Belt of the Serpent</u></b></i><br /> Artifact ooo<br /> Attunement 5m<br /> <br /> <i>Made for the Grand Enlightened Master of the Snake centuries ago, this wondrous and yet wicked looking belt woven of snake leathers, green jade, and oricalcum, bears a snake head with two emerald eyes, and it fastens by sinking its teeth into its own tail. It seems to shift ever so slightly in dim light or shadows, and it moves in oddly sinuous ways when shaken or jostled. </i><br /> <br /> When attuned to the <i>Belt of the Serpent</i>, you may use Mastery keywords for charms in the Snake Style. If you are a Terrestrial, you may ignore the Terrestrial keyword of charms in the Snake Style.<br /> - - - -<br /> There, that wasn't so hard. It will make a Snake Style DB considerably more powerful, but probably only to the extent that grabbing an Artifact Weapon would to any other DB. You can easily whip one of these up for any other style, and if it turns out to be too powerful, separate the Mastery ability and the Terrestrial ability and put one of them behind a vision quest or something. Fighting the embodiment of Snake Style to prove you are worthy of the belt is sick as fuck.<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>Fan of the Crane</b><br /> <b>Tattoo of the Centipede</b><br /> <b>Necklace of the Tiger</b><br /> <b>Eye of the Burning Judge</b></u></i><br /> <br /> Tada, you did it.<br /> <br /> Its important that the <i><u><b>Whatever of the Animal</b></u></i> isn't a weapon or armor because it would be too much powerful for too little cost. Also you get a mini-quest where you have to prove yourself against the embodiment of a style and must defeat the Concept of Snake using snake martial arts and if you don't think thats the most Exalted shit ever report to the morgue because you have no soul.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually now i'm hooked on it. <br /> <br /> <u><b>VISION QUEST</b></u><br /> So taking Snake Style as an example, what are some quick snapshots the themes of Snake Style MA? Dodge, Armor Piercing, Poisons. <br /> <br /> So you meditate and perform a ritual and light some sacred incense and then enter the Mental Realm of the Dojo of the Snake. Before you is a Giant Serpent. The snake doesn't fight you using snake style, thats your job, the snake instead fights like a big snake, <i>with strengths designed to be specifically countered by Snake Style</i>. <br /> <br /> It has tough scales, you need to use Armor Penetrating Fang Strike. <br /> It heals rapidly from all wounds/ moves in an out of range swiftly until you cripple or poison it. <br /> The snake makes a big damage, low accuracy unblockable attack, so you must be constantly dodging it. <br /> <br /> There, you now have a Final Exam Boss Fight that is designed to prove you are worthy of unlocking the power of the Snake. <br /> <br /> Tiger? You have to hunt the master hunter. <br /> Crane? You must avoid being hit while engaging in a philosophical debate.<br /> Centipede? you have to get a dustpan and broom and release them outside idk i havent read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 07-25-2020, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T20:17:49-07:00","id":1404697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404689#post1404689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b><u>Belt of the Serpent</u></b></i><br /> Artifact ooo<br /> Attunement 5m<br /> <br /> There, that wasn't so hard. It will make a Snake Style DB considerably more powerful, but probably only to the extent that grabbing an Artifact Weapon would to any other DB.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main thing I worry about is &quot;an artifact weapon&quot; is one of the strongest effects in the game. If you could repeatedly commit 5m for +1 accuracy, +3 damage, +2-4 overwhelming I imagine the optimal character would get 10 or so of them, depending on essence. (unless solar alpha-strikes were coming into play and you expected a fight to be over before you make a withering attack). This isn't scary because it's stronger than an artifact weapon, it's scary because you can combine it with an artifact weapon, and you can't combine two artifact weapons (well, you can't combine their stat boosts on a single attack. You can obviously hold two artifact weapons at the same time)<br /> <br /> Which makes me think of something that would make me a lot more comfortable with anything that removed the terrestrial keyword or added the mastery keyword semi-permanently - banning it from combination with artifact weapons. Or, more thematically, forcing it to be used unarmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T21:14:37-07:00","id":1404704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404697#post1404697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main thing I worry about is &quot;an artifact weapon&quot; is one of the strongest effects in the game. If you could repeatedly commit 5m for +1 accuracy, +3 damage, +2-4 overwhelming I imagine the optimal character would get 10 or so of them, depending on essence. (unless solar alpha-strikes were coming into play and you expected a fight to be over before you make a withering attack). This isn't scary because it's stronger than an artifact weapon, it's scary because you can combine it with an artifact weapon, and you can't combine two artifact weapons (well, you can't combine their stat boosts on a single attack. You can obviously hold two artifact weapons at the same time)<br /> <br /> Which makes me think of something that would make me a lot more comfortable with anything that removed the terrestrial keyword or added the mastery keyword semi-permanently - banning it from combination with artifact weapons. Or, more thematically, forcing it to be used unarmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, the artifacts could be weapons that explicitly use mundane stats and which only grant mastery when wielded. This would allow weapon-only styles like Single Point to have one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T23:45:57-07:00","id":1404716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404689#post1404689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b><u>Belt of the Serpent</u></b></i><br /> <br /> There, that wasn't so hard. It will make a Snake Style DB considerably more powerful, but probably only to the extent that grabbing an Artifact Weapon would to any other DB. You can easily whip one of these up for any other style, and if it turns out to be too powerful, separate the Mastery ability and the Terrestrial ability and put one of them behind a vision quest or something. Fighting the embodiment of Snake Style to prove you are worthy of the belt is sick as fuck.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is also way too easy to do... in short the benefit is far greater than the cost.<br /> <br /> 3 dot artifacts don't really do much more than what a character of sufficient skill would be able to do. If we treat the normal effects of Martial Art Charms as the baseline, then a 3 dot artifact shouldn't produce an effect any greater than that... and the Mastery effects, are by definition, greater than what is normally possible by the Charms usual effects. Thus any artifact that would allow for Mastery effects to be possible would need to be at least a 4 dot artifact and such artifacts should at least feel as they are providing a benefit that is somewhat beyond what a character could normally do.<br /> <br /> All you have really done is slap on a 3 dot artifact and BOOM! any Exalt can now use Mastery effects... even if you have to create a &quot;unique&quot; for such artifacts depending upon the Martial Art in question. It really comes down to balancing the extraordinary effort that non-Solar/Sidereal Exalts have to go through to achieve this result while not making it so easy that Mastery effectively becomes meaningless.<br /> <br /> The artifact should feel like it is a benefit to any Exalt that uses it, regardless of whether or not they can naturally access Mastery effects or are subject to Terrestrial limitations. That this also unlocks the Mastery effects of charms for other Exalts is a secondary effect that, while significant, isn't overly game breaking... especially if there are limitations to when those effects can be used... such as the need to be under the effects of a Form Charm or can only be used with unarmed strikes or such.<br /> <br /> Now let's take the Perfected Kata Bracers that JohnDoe244 provided us information on and see if we can't find a way for it to work in 3rd Ed and feel like they are a proper 4 dot artifact. For the base effect of these Bracers, I don't see why we don't stick to the one described in 2nd Eddition... specifically adding Essence to the Accuracy, Damage and Defense of Unarmed and Form Weapons attacks when under the effect of a Form Charm. Yes, this does sound quite potent at first blush, but look at it from a wider perspective... of what it means for starting characters as well as advanced ones. Many starting Exalts will only have a starting Essence of 1 and it will be quite a few sessions before they reach Essence 2 and even longer for higher Essence levels. By the time they get up to Essence 5 or higher, this bonus while still significant is not as spectacular as many of the other effects that most characters will have. This effect is also fairly limited in scope and duration... to just a small selection of weapons (and their artifact equivalents) and unarmed attacks for at most a scene... and while it can change the style of play dramatically, it usually will not have a long lasting effect outside of the current scene. Overall, these bracers don't actually do more than what the character would have been able to do with their own charms (Excellencies can easily make weapons more accurate and increase defenses for example). To limit the abuse that this bonus can cause, we could say that these are counted as dice added by Charms, thus limiting how much more can be added by other Charms.<br /> <br /> Now, the 2nd Edition version had additional benefits that were added due to the material they were made from. Magical Materials in 3rd Edition doesn't do this anymore... so this is where we could add the effect that allows a user to nullify the effects of Terrestrial Keywords and/or unlock the Mastery effects of charms. Of course, for it to remain an attractive choice for characters that normally have access to Mastery Effects, there should still be some benefit for them as well... and the Starmetal effect seems like a nice bonus for such characters... a 2 mote reduction in costs (to a minimum of 1 mote) for all style Charms while under the effect of a Form Charm. Still... having both this and the above effect automatically active does seem a little too easy overall. Perhaps a small cost to activate this effect is called for... such as the spending of 1 Willpower to show the level of concentration and mental taxing producing this side effect is... especially if one has to pay it again if they change forms (thus forcing a potentially difficult choice upon characters that know multiple forms as to which Mastery effects they wish to use; or which Martial Arts charms they want to use at a lesser cost for Solars/Sidereal).<br /> <br /> Now, lastly, comes the balancing act... specifically any additional drawbacks to using this artifact. The most significant will be the cost to attune to the artifact. Like in 2nd Ed, I feel that 8 motes is fair, as this is the general commitment one pays for most Form Charms (some are higher, some are lower, so this is the rough average). Combined with the costs of the Form Charm (which is committed as well), and this ties up a fair bit of motes from the character's Essence Pools that can not be regained until the commitment is allowed to elapse. The other significant drawback of the 2nd Edition version was the glowing that the bracers produce... a clear display of supernatural power that identified the character as a significant threat. Again, I don't see why this should change... though we do need to take into account that 3rd Edition has effects that can use Anima levels for various effects. Using these bracers will definitely make it quite obvious to all that the user is using a supernatural effect, thus I would say that it causes an Exalt's anima to flare at least to the Burning level... nullifying any stealth effects that the character may have been using. Additionally, should the character's Anima drop bellow Glowing, they are no longer considered to be under the effects of a Form Charm and loose any benefit they may have had as such (including from the Bracers)... at least until such time as they re-establish the use of their Form Charm (basically, if they drop to a Dim Anima, they loose commitment of their Form Charm until the cost to enter it is payed again). In short, to keep the benefits of the Bracers, they must remain fairly obvious to those observing the combat.<br /> <br /> Now, when taken as a whole, this feels like a fairly potent artifact. Even for a starting character, they will have some significant bonuses and can unlock some potent effects through Mastery (if they didn't have it) or a cost break (if they naturally have access to Mastery effects). As the character grows more powerful, these bonuses grow with them, though not beyond what one would expect overall. It also encourages a specific style of play... namely staying within a single Form, but doesn't prevent one from doing otherwise (it only limits which Mastery effects one has access to at a given moment, though it is still possible, if costly, to switch if one needs to). It also makes one a rather obvious target to enemies, and any attempts to mitigate this effect could see the loss of the benefits one gains. One is showing off their combat prowess... to hide that would be counter-productive. Add the commitment cost to attune and the Willpower cost to unlock the Mastery effects (and ignore Terrestrial limitations) and I think we have a fairly balanced 4 dot artifact that provides a fair advantage, unique play style, fair costs for the gains received, and reasonable drawbacks that a Storyteller can use keep the player from abusing their new power too much (when done fairly). There is a clear reason why a given player might want this for their martial artist character, but also clear reasons why they might pass it up too (especially for more ninja stealth fighter types who don't want to draw attention to their fights).<br /> <br /> Give me a day or two and I will do a more formal write-up of this version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T00:37:02-07:00","id":1404720,"title":"","content":"I mean, it makes DB martials arts really viable and.... yeah thats it. At E2 a DB can have 7 charms from Snake including the Form Charm. Lets take a quick survey of Mastery and Terrestrial keywords in Snake:<br /> <br /> <b>Serpentine Evasion- </b>Mastery- makes the charm go from 2m to 1m each time you use it after the first time each turn. it saves you a single mote on repeated dodges. <br /> <b>Striking Cobra- </b>Mastery<b>- </b>you add (Ess+2) to your initiative for the purpose of activating this charm (requires being higher initiative than opponent). <br /> <b>Armor Penetrating Fang Strike</b>- Terrestrial- lets you ignore the reset condition (which is land a decisive and get to 12+ initiative) <br /> <b>Crippling Pressure Point Strike</b>- Terrestrial- a meaty one. DBs can only use this charm after a dodge, and they can't use a difficulty 6 gambit to paralyze an opponents legs. <br /> <b>Essence Fang And Scales</b>- Mastery- adds 2 to decisive damage<br /> <b>Uncoiling Serpent Prana</b>-Terrestrial- lets them combo this with Essence Fangs to grab people out to medium range and Scorpion pull them over to you. <br /> <br /> I think thats enough of for now. Only the Decisive damage bonus stands out to me as a big deal, followed by Armor Penetrating Fang Strike being usable more often (ignores Soak from armor and Ess or 3 hardness). <br /> <br /> Yeah that's good, but is that <i>significantly</i> better than taking an artifact weapon for Snake (hook sword and sectional staff)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T01:39:33-07:00","id":1404728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404689#post1404689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b><u>Belt of the Serpent</u></b></i><br /> Artifact ooo<br /> Attunement 5m<br /> <br /> <i>Made for the Grand Enlightened Master of the Snake centuries ago, this wondrous and yet wicked looking belt woven of snake leathers, green jade, and oricalcum, bears a snake head with two emerald eyes, and it fastens by sinking its teeth into its own tail. It seems to shift ever so slightly in dim light or shadows, and it moves in oddly sinuous ways when shaken or jostled. </i><br /> <br /> When attuned to the <i>Belt of the Serpent</i>, you may use Mastery keywords for charms in the Snake Style. If you are a Terrestrial, you may ignore the Terrestrial keyword of charms in the Snake Style.<br /> - - - -<br /> There, that wasn't so hard. It will make a Snake Style DB considerably more powerful, but probably only to the extent that grabbing an Artifact Weapon would to any other DB. You can easily whip one of these up for any other style, and if it turns out to be too powerful, separate the Mastery ability and the Terrestrial ability and put one of them behind a vision quest or something. Fighting the embodiment of Snake Style to prove you are worthy of the belt is sick as fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that scans.<br /> <br /> The problem is not &quot;is it less powerful than an artifact form weapon&quot;, but &quot;how does this stack with an artifact form weapon&quot;.<br /> <br /> A single martial arts style seems within the confines of Artifact 3. I'd limit it to bumping you up one step: Terrestrial to Neutral, Neutral to Mastery.<br /> <br /> For folks who already have Mastery, I'd look at having it bump Resonance up one step with the Style's Form Weapons. For Solars, I'd let them wear this unattuned in order to <i>look metal</i>.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I'd have it grant Mastery (even to Terrestrials) with Serpentine Evasion and Striking Cobra Technique on attunement, and have a Permenant Evocation (no mote cost) which expanded this to the entire style when in Snake Form.<br /> <br /> Alternate alternatively, have it grant Mastery but only when using unarmed strikes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404704#post1404704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively, the artifacts could be weapons that explicitly use mundane stats and which only grant mastery when wielded. This would allow weapon-only styles like Single Point to have one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404650#post1404650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> Thanks for the information on the 2nd Ed Perfected Kata Bracers.<br /> <br /> As for your take on them for 3rd Ed... it is a little lack-luster in my opinion.<br /> <br /> The two Exalts that are normally resonant with this artifact to get the benefit of 3 of the 4 Evocations (in other words don't need to wait until Essence 2+ to learn them) have no need for those Evocations as they naturally have access to the Mastery Keyword and are not subject to the Terrestrial Keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps some commentary here.<br /> <br /> Firstly, we don't know how Sidereals will access Mastery, but the devs have suggested they won't just get it.<br /> <br /> Secondly Lunars have a Charm which drops their affinity for artifacts one step: it doesn't strike me as beyond the realm of possibility to have a Solar Charm which did likewise.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, the Magical Materials Benefits were written (as with most of my custom artifacts) with Exingents in mind.<br /> <br /> You'll note the Evocation tree is flat. You don't have to buy Evocations which aren't useful to you.<br /> <br /> The Essence minimums were not chosen at random. A 14 year old DB in secondary school should not be rocking Mastery effects beyond an Immaculate Master. A starting PC could be. Solars, Sidereals and Exingents with an affinity for Martial Arts have every right to be (Solars shouldn't need this artifact to get there, but if someone invents a custom Martial Art that doesn't yield naturally to Solars, Solars shouldn't be the only ones left in the cold when it comes to boosting one's proficiency). Which drops us to Lunar Martial Artists: as they can combine their native Charms with Martial Arts, and this already puts them on a par with Mastery users, I don't think it's appropriate to give them Mastery from character creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the last of the 4 Evocations, the one that is automatically learned, again, the Solars and Sidereal have more efficient means of gaining a success or raising their Parry than a 3 mote cost effect. </div> </div> </div>Solars and Sidereals are getting the Resonant bonus of raising their Parry/Successes by 2 for 3m, and Aggravated damage, and Flurry penalty reduction.<br /> <br /> You have every right not to like my work, but please hate what I actually wrote.<br /> <br /> (That said, I wouldn't be opposed to granting the Flexible tag to attacks as well.)<br /> <br /> The effort here was not to provide all things to all men, but to have an artifact which wouldn't horribly skew the game when added to artifact form weapons and met the idea of providing Mastery to users which lacked it.<br /> <br /> If you already have Mela's Coil, then Four Dot Razor Claws isn't going to change your playstyle.<br /> If you already have Mastery, then an Artifact which grants Mastery isn't going to change your playstyle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for other Exalts, it is rather over-punishing for little real gain. </div> </div> </div>Go back to your Hearthstone thread and read what just about every other ST said about granting the Mastery keyword to non-Solars. I'll wait.<br /> <br /> You might not think it's a big deal, but trust me, it's a big deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only one type of Exalt really needs the Evocation that allows one to ignore the effects of the Terrestrial Keyword... Dragon-Bloods. </div> </div> </div>Good job that Evocation isn't a prerequisite for the other powers then, right?<br /> <br /> (Also Liminals, Exingents, and Alchemicals. And demons, god-blooded, terrestrial gods/elementals, and enlightened martial artists who somehow gained an Essence pool.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beyond that, you have rather steep costs for the three Evocations +5 motes and 1 or 2 Willpower, thus a Dragon-Blooded will be spending a significant portion of their Essence Pool (10 motes) and force of will (1 or 2 Willpower) just to access the relatively minor gains that Mastery provides... and only so long as they are able to remain under the effects of a Form Charm. </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Immaculate Masters always have the option of expending Aura. But we're talking scene long Mastery here.<br /> <br /> Compare to second edition, which required Essence 3, Martial Arts 3, a refined diet and two Charms (which each cost 50% more than normal Charms) just to shake the Terrestial limitation. They had no way of getting on par with Solars, and even after that still had to roll or risk messing up every time they used a Form Charm.<br /> <br /> Compare with the current rules: learn five Charms, enter a Martial Arts Form, AND expend Aura to ignore the Terrrestrial keyword for a single tick. One Evocation and 5m to ignore it for the whole scene is a bargain.<br /> <br /> Going beyond your natural limits is hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It really puts a lot of hurdles that have to be overcome so that most Exalts have to pay prohibitive amounts to access fairly minor effects (in respect to the cost paid). It honestly looks like it is designed more to punish a player than to reward them with a new style of play. </div> </div> </div>A new style of play shouldn't be a straight upgrade.<br /> <br /> There should be a trade-off. (Don't forget the 3m attunement cost -- I balanced this on 13m 2WP to give DBs Mastery.)<br /> <br /> After play begins, Artiacts are a Story merit. They are free. They are a reward the ST gives the players. They can also be crafted (trivially, with Solar Charms).<br /> <br /> I envisage this artifact being won from an old master, liberated from the body of a demon, stolen from a forgotten tomb or forged by an ally.<br /> <br /> Then Dragon-XP can be used to buy the Evocations and Martial Arts Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404716#post1404716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the base effect of these Bracers, I don't see why we don't stick to the one described in 2nd Eddition... specifically adding Essence to the Accuracy, Damage and Defense of Unarmed and Form Weapons attacks when under the effect of a Form Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>An always on, +1-5/+2-10 bonus in the style of the 2E artifact is hideodiously broken under the 3E paradigm. Even as a Charm bonus for 8m commitment, in Form only. Resting Parry 10, rising to 14 at Essence 5, is a hard &quot;no&quot;. (2E was &quot;balanced&quot; around &quot;perfect or die&quot; -- bigger numbers were cool but didn't rock that paradigm. 2.5 had specific rules to stop you stacking bigger numbers. And even then, Perfected Kata Bracers had questionable balance. Even cutting the bonus in half with 3E's lower Essence scores doesn't make this artifact work as a straight port.)<br /> <br /> I might suggest having it simply upgrade one's unarmed attacks to use the traits of Artifact weapons instead; but <i>that</i> would be a four dot artifact of itself (like how Silken Armor allows you to use artifact armor on your martial arts). Adding Mastery on top of that artifact would push it to high 5-dot/low N/A territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-27-2020, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T05:01:34-07:00","id":1404750,"title":"","content":"Personally I don't like the idea of granting a unique trait of some of the most powerful beings in Exalted to others through artifacts or hearthstone. I wouldn't grant Supernals this way either and Exalted agrees with me(just look at how the glory stone, a greater hearthstone, operates as this is about as good as it gets). I wouldn't give Lunar shape shifting or Sidereal martial arts to others, not including Solars who can learn them. The things that are unique to each type are exalted are unique for a reason. <br /> If I we're going to allow a player to gain something like this I'd probably use a sorcerous working altering the nature of the being in question and only upgrading their capability. A DB for instance, would lose Terrestrial keywords on martial arts charms and when expending aura after learning the form charm of an Immaculate style would get access to the mastery keyword. The working should be unique requiring different ingredients as it is a personalized change, this keeps you from having a few hundred mastery using Exalted running around that aren't Solars or Sidereals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","user":"Arkayriel","date":". 07-26-2020, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T19:05:15-07:00","id":1404862,"title":"","content":"Mastery is cool but I wouldn't call it the unique property of Solars. Its just a facet of their &quot;amazing at everything&quot; diamond. <br /> <br /> Martial Arts is a weird overlapping circle because Martial Arts don't &quot;belong&quot; to any exalted type, its a side thing they all share. And if a DB needs an artifact just to be able to do that one specific thing as well as a Solar can just by existing, I think that's fine. Consider that the Solar has more motes, better excellencies, better everything else. A combat focused Snake Style DB with Belt of the Serpent is going to be as good as a Twilight or Eclipse who splashed Snake on the side. They're gonna be crushed by a Dawn MA Supernal who started the game with Snake mastered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T21:22:07-07:00","id":1404875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404862#post1404862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mastery is cool but I wouldn't call it the unique property of Solars. Its just a facet of their &amp;quot;amazing at everything&amp;quot; diamond. <br /> <br /> Martial Arts is a weird overlapping circle because Martial Arts don't &amp;quot;belong&amp;quot; to any exalted type, its a side thing they all share. And if a DB needs an artifact just to be able to do that one specific thing as well as a Solar can just by existing, I think that's fine. Consider that the Solar has more motes, better excellencies, better everything else. A combat focused Snake Style DB with Belt of the Serpent is going to be as good as a Twilight or Eclipse who splashed Snake on the side. They're gonna be crushed by a Dawn MA Supernal who started the game with Snake mastered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, fair point on it not being unique if Exigents get a way to get mastery. I was thinking of Infernals and Abyssals as basically Solars and Sidereals are the masters of martial arts and also cheater mccheatersons so I was thinking that way. But sure, I'll concede that.<br /> <br /> I also forgot to put in a little part about how I wouldn't do it as an artifact unless we it was a powerful and unique one. The reason isn't power balance. If you make it to easy it diminishes what the DB accomplishes by getting the mastery effect. I want to tell stories about my PCs awesome accomplishments not how they are like everyone else. That's why it's a personal choice for me to use a working instead. If my players just want the mechanically best martial artist, I'd work at convincing them to play a Solar or Sidereal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T12:52:34-07:00","id":1404963,"title":"","content":"This is curious, because I was actually working on a redesign of Perfected Kata Bracers myself. They're incredibly rough drafted, and probably super broken, as I was messing around with mechanics and haven't had a chance to test them, but it might be something you were looking towards.<br /> <br /> Essentially, rather then just making a stat-stick to beat people with, which is what old Perfected Kata Bracers were, I wanted to make something that was engaging and would want to be picked up by Martial Arts Masters; that they were weapons for people who picked up two or three martial arts and designed their fighting style around combining them together. In that vein, rather then just making it give you the Mastery keyword or anything, I made specifically synergistic charms that work off of combining the base martial arts.<br /> <br /> I also experimented with taking Style points from 2E's Cobra style, where you get them for playing into your chosen style's gameplan and spend them for benefits, and the Innate keyword, which was a keyword in the original Evocation drafts where you could permanently learn charms from Evocations. I took that same basic idea, but played around with how a charm becomes innate; some are free, some are repurchases, sometimes the effect is weaker without the bracers.<br /> <br /> They're very rough draft because I haven't really gone over them in quite a few months and most likely very, very unbalanced (just as a whole, I think my Homebrew tends towards incredibly overpowered because I'm a fan of flashy effects and combos), but I'm willing enough to share them.<br /> <br /> The First one I made was for Black Claw, White Veil, and Ebon Shadow: Even looking at it now some of the style points aren't exactly understandable with what this is supposed to be, as it mentions using a weapon. I think, in the idea me and the person who helped me spitball these ideas had, was that they actively turned your Unarmed attacks into Light Artifact Weapons (Which goes against the idea of a stat-stick, but in our games we've found Overwhelming to be so important that bare fists without any way to raise your Overwhelming can leave you pretty useless in most fights), but I assume from how I've written it, you could still pick up and use a different weapon if you wanted to; which is why there is a note about Table Turning Reversal; I guess in case you just felt like instead swiping a Daiklave from your opponent instead of using your fists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H6GaG8ay2rj7krn8ehtO4QB5h9A-EuBM3qK3Q0o5ffY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H6GaG8ay2rj7krn8ehtO4QB5h9A-EuBM3qK3Q0o5ffY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H6GaG8ay2rj7krn8ehtO4QB5h9A-EuBM3qK3Q0o5ffY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1H6GaG8ay2rj7krn8ehtO4QB5h9A-EuBM3qK3Q0o5ffY/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The second one (that I will eventually be playtesting and attempting to refine more) is for Fire Dragon, Steel Devil, and Snake:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WFcTz9AmkUhac1Hbf0am7gNAVMH6kng9iX7tX9p7DGQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WFcTz9AmkUhac1Hbf0am7gNAVMH6kng9iX7tX9p7DGQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WFcTz9AmkUhac1Hbf0am7gNAVMH6kng9iX7tX9p7DGQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WFcTz9AmkUhac1Hbf0am7gNAVMH6kng9iX7tX9p7DGQ/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I had a few other ideas that aren't anymore then rough outlines for stuff like a Golden Janissary, White Reaper, and Laughing Monster combination that's a Staff.<br /> <br /> I don't know if this helps you or not, but it's something I was working on in trying to figure out a way to make combining martial arts engaging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T17:32:23-07:00","id":1404992,"title":"","content":"What are people\u2019s thoughts on an Evocation for a DB-focused Perfected Kata Bracers adding (Essence) non-Charm dice (or (Essence/2, rounded down) Parry) on a full Excellency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T18:12:34-07:00","id":1404999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404992#post1404992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are people\u2019s thoughts on an Evocation for a DB-focused Perfected Kata Bracers adding (Essence) non-Charm dice (or (Essence/2, rounded down) Parry) on a full Excellency?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's meant to work like an Excellency (usable at will, pay 1m/die) then I'd limit the total of this plus the DB's base Excellency to +10 (or +5 Parry) on principle.<br /> <br /> Between the Mastery tag and boosting the Excellency, this raises the wielder to Celestial power level in combat, so it's important to make sure a combatant with this level of power fits in the game where you want to use this Evocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T05:02:27-07:00","id":1405048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhanjRho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1404992#post1404992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are people\u2019s thoughts on an Evocation for a DB-focused Perfected Kata Bracers adding (Essence) non-Charm dice (or (Essence/2, rounded down) Parry) on a full Excellency?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends what else the Bracers are doing. <br /> <br /> If you're using my idea and threw a modest mote cost (2m, say) on this Evocation AND it was only usable on a Full Excellency then I'd be fine with that -- a DB is going to tap out pretty quick if she's blowing 8m on every roll. I like the idea of a DB burning bright for one brief moment.<br /> <br /> If you're using Shadowstripe's idea and this Evocation is meant to be a free bonus, then you've just given DBs Mastery and Solar-esque dice pools. If you want to play a Solar, just play a Solar: DBs are meant to be weaker than Solars, that's the point of them.<br /> <br /> I would be reluctant to have (Essence) non-Charm dice on an Artifact not pitched at DBs. Solars really don't need to be throwing another 5 dice on their attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T23:05:13-07:00","id":1405130,"title":"","content":"It has taken a little longer for me to come up with my take on the Perfected Kata Bracers than I intended, but here is what I have come up with.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><i>Perfected Kata Bracers</i></b> (Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <br /> It has long been forgotten who forged the first of these bracers. While each reflects the Master who made them, they also reflect the simplicity of the first of their kind. Each takes the form of a prayer strip made from one of the magical materials (except Starmetal) that have been twisted to fit around the forearms or calves of an individual. Engraved into each are a series of sutras that have been inlaid with Starmetal. Sidereal Exalts are always considered to resonate with these bracers regardless of what material they are made from (as all of them use Starmetal). Attunement costs is 8 motes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><u>Evocations of the Perfected Kata Bracers</u></b> </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Blossoming of the Lotus</b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>None<br /> <br /> When the wearer of these bracers uses the Form Charm of a Martial Art, they can activate this Evocation at the cost of 1 willpower. Doing so allows the wearer to access the effects of the Mastery Keyword for any Charm within the style of the Form they are in for as long as they remain in that Form. Additionally, while this Evocation is active, the wearer may ignore any instance of the Terrestrial Keyword for any charm in their current Form\u2019s style that might apply to the wearer.<br /> <br /> For those Exalts that can naturally access the effects of the Mastery Keyword, this Evocation instead allows the wearer to draw upon the natural Essence of the world around them to reduce the cost of all Charms within the style of the Form Charm by 2 motes (to a minimum of 1 mote per effect).<br /> <br /> When this Evocation is active, the Starmetal sutras glow with a bight light that forces the wearer\u2019s Anima to flare to the Burning level of display. Should the wearer activate a Charm with an Anima cost that reduces the Anima display to the Dim level for longer than the end of their next turn, this Evocation\u2019s effect ends and the wearer looses any benefit of their Form Charm until such time as they can activate it again. Otherwise, this Evocation lasts for as long as they remain under the effect of their current Form Charm (switching forms requires this Evocation to be activated again to gain its benefits with the new style\u2019s charms).<br /> <br /> This Evocation is unlocked at no cost the first time an attuned wearer enters a Martial Arts Form.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Perfected Kata Strike</b></span><br /> <b>Cost: </b>(Essence) motes (+1 wp); <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Blossoming of the Lotus<br /> <br /> This Evocation allows the wearer to enhance an unarmed or style weapon strike with extraordinary precision while using a Form Charm. When the wearer prepares to finish off their opponent, they add their Essence rating to the Accuracy and Damage of a Decisive attack. The wearer can choose to do either Bashing or Lethal damage regardless of what damage type their attack normally does. If the wearer is fighting a Creature of Darkness (or a Fair Folk), they can spend 1 Willpower to make the damage done Aggravated.<br /> <br /> <b>Special activation rules: </b>This Evocation awakens at no cost when the wielder, who must have been attuned for at least one story, is engaged with a Creature of Darkness (or Fair Folk) with an Essence rating higher than theirs (maximum of 5) and defeats that foe or emerges from Initiative Crash that the foe caused them to suffer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not entirely sure how well the second evocation compares with the effects of the Charms that a given Martial Artist will have thanks to the effects of the first evocation... so I may still tweek it as needed to better balance it (as in it is an alternative strike rather than a superior one). That it can deal Aggravated damage (to Creatures of Darkness and Fair Folk) I think makes it something a player would consider in some circumstances as don't recall many Martial Art Charms allowing for such damage in most uses. I may give it the Dual Keyword instead of the Decisive-Only and have the Decisive effect deal Aggravated damage regardless of the opponent... but in that case I think the cost of using the Evocation will need to be higher, at least when a Decisive attack is made. Might also increase the Essence minimum as well. As it is, it is intended to be more effective the more experienced the Exalt is and thus more costly to use (one can not choose to pay less for a lesser effect... it is all or nothing). Additionally, since the Evocation isn't part of any Style, it will not benefit from the reduced Charm cost that natural Masters get when using the first Evocation's effects.<br /> <br /> As you can see, overall this Artifact is useful to anyone who acquires it, whether they are natural Martial Art Masters or not... and does provide clear play style that many Exalt types would not normally have (specifically Mastery Keyword effects). One does have some hurdles to overcome to awaken the evocations, but the balancing point is the cost of using the Evocations rather than more hurdles to overcome to gain the rewards of owning so powerful an artifact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T05:52:56-07:00","id":1405153,"title":"","content":"I still feel a DB with a non-immaculate Martial Art will always get this Artifact if they are able (with some exceptions such as Ebon Shadow or White Veil which would be terrible with it).<br /> <br /> That said it's got the feel of a proper artifact, and I can see it fitting just fine in the right games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T08:20:17-07:00","id":1405160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1405153#post1405153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still feel a DB with a non-immaculate Martial Art will always get this Artifact if they are able (with some exceptions such as Ebon Shadow or White Veil which would be terrible with it).<br /> <br /> That said it's got the feel of a proper artifact, and I can see it fitting just fine in the right games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably that's why there no official artifact that does that. Still is a great idea for a PC who wants to become a master martial artist and shouldn't be a lot of them with the same exact evocations (I can even consider every one being only applicable for one or two styles and having not so generic powers to begin with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2896-nemastoncito","name":"Nemastoncito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T16:25:17-07:00","id":1405215,"title":"","content":"I was honestly debating whether or not to treat the effects as innate abilities or as evocations. I opted for expressing them as evocations only because there are too few artifacts that have innate abilities that are powered through Essence (or Willpower), especially when they have more than one effect. Since I wanted to keep the feel of the original inspiration and add the secondary effect that allows access to the Mastery Keyword, evocations seemed the best way to display that.<br /> <br /> That said, whether they actually are Evocations or just expressed through a similar mechanic is a matter of debate. While no two artifacts are exactly alike, quite a few have been copied and their effects replicated. True, most of these are of the 2 Dot variety, but the fairly simplistic design of the Perfected Kata Bracers suggests that they not difficult to make overall, but they do have to be... well... perfect. The reason they are considered 4 dots is due to the exacting precision needed to produce them... even the slightest flaw could ruin months, if not years of work making one (and very likely can only be constructed by those who are natural Masters of the Martial Arts)... plus the effects are substantial (though whether they are powerful is a subjective decision).<br /> <br /> Even so, they do have limitations... namely that the effects only work when one is using a Form Charm and even then the effects only apply to charms that belong in the same Style as that Form Charm. In other words, you can't access the Mastery effects of Tiger Style when you are in Snake Form... or the Mastery effects of Snake Style when in in Tiger Form. That changing from one Form to another requires one to pay the Willpower cost to access the Mastery effects will put some limits on how powerful the user will be. Sure, they may still freely combine Martial Art charms as always, but they will only be able to benefit from the Mastery effects of the charms from the style they are currently in Form for. Lastly... glowing like a beacon for all to see will tend to make one a target of interest for most groups... and will likely be perceived as a threat by most opponents. This means that they are more likely to be attacked by multiple opponents (with the bonuses and penalties there in applying).<br /> <br /> In short, it will be up to the Storyteller any player alike to take full advantage of everything these Bracers provide... both mechanically and from a role-playing perspective. It will be a balancing act of course, but when done right it will create situations where the player can truly shine (though when done wrong it can leave the player either feeling overwhelmed and unduly burdened or just not properly challenged). It is also very likely that at some point, other Martial Artists will learn of their ability and seek to challenge the owner... especially if they are suspicious of what they have in their possession. Basically, those who possess such an artifact are likely to lead some rather interesting lives.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T03:31:44-07:00","id":1405292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1405048#post1405048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends what else the Bracers are doing.<br /> <br /> If you're using my idea and threw a modest mote cost (2m, say) on this Evocation AND it was only usable on a Full Excellency then I'd be fine with that -- a DB is going to tap out pretty quick if she's blowing 8m on every roll. I like the idea of a DB burning bright for one brief moment.<br /> <br /> If you're using Shadowstripe's idea and this Evocation is meant to be a free bonus, then you've just given DBs Mastery and Solar-esque dice pools. If you want to play a Solar, just play a Solar: DBs are meant to be weaker than Solars, that's the point of them.<br /> <br /> I would be reluctant to have (Essence) non-Charm dice on an Artifact not pitched at DBs. Solars really don't need to be throwing another 5 dice on their attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that the full write-up I provided has shown that you made some false assumptions of my intent.<br /> <br /> I wasn't trying to make Dragon-Blooded into the equivalent of Solars (in fact, I wasn't thinking of Dragon-Blooded at all when I started looking into this... I was actually aiming more towards Lunar Martial Artists to be honest). I also had every intent on doing this in such a way as to preserve Solar supremacy with Martial Arts by limiting just how much access one has to Mastery effects and under what conditions one can access such effects. The Solar position as the true Masters of the Martial Arts remains untouched... even if they aren't using this artifact and are fighting someone who is using it. I also wanted to create an artifact that even Solars and Sidereal would want to use, even if they don't need it to access Mastery effects. Finally, I wanted to make sure that the costs of using this artifact were equal to the benefits one gained by using it... something I felt that was not well thought out in your original version (very high costs and lots of hoops to jump through for a gain that didn't feel worth the price). True, my impression of your version of the bracers is a subjective one.... but one I feel is accurate (how many players in your games have asked for your version of the bracers... or how many of your own characters use it?).<br /> <br /> All that said, I am still not entirely sure I balanced my version well enough... especially with the second Evocation (feels a little... meh... to me). I am curious as to your opinion now that you can more clearly see what I am aiming for with this artifact. As for the bonus dice added, I have been operating under the impression that all bonuses added through the expenditure of essence are considered Charm bonuses by default (even when not provided by Charms)... so I have no idea how you got the impression that the bonuses would be considered non-Charm. Everything I have read points to this as the default assumption (though I do admit I may have overlooked or misread something). If I have, then it is an easy enough fix to state that the bonuses are considered Charm-based bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T08:25:02-07:00","id":1405342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1405292#post1405292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the bonus dice added, I have been operating under the impression that all bonuses added through the expenditure of essence are considered Charm bonuses by default (even when not provided by Charms)... so I have no idea how you got the impression that the bonuses would be considered non-Charm. Everything I have read points to this as the default assumption (though I do admit I may have overlooked or misread something). If I have, then it is an easy enough fix to state that the bonuses are considered Charm-based bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>The post from JohnDoe244 you're quoting was directed at GhanjRho, who was asking whether an Evocation that gives (Essence) non-charm dice on the bracers was a good idea.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T10:39:28-07:00","id":1405386,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd rather have mastery accessible through some inner power/charm, not through an artifact (which is basically cheating and going &quot;yeah, they suck without MAGIC SOLAR HAX&quot;)<br /> <br /> My Water-Aspect, Nellens Suguha, eventually gains a charm in my vague mind-game that I work on whenever I'm bored through learning all five IMA and then using that and a Celestial Working (I should mention at this point that she can use Celestial spells too natively) to give her a permanent charm that makes her automatically ignore the Terrestrial keyword on her MA and upgrades the &quot;burn aura to ignore Terrestrial&quot; to &quot;burn aura to access Mastery effect&quot;. It also causes <i>all</i> her IMA to gain Mastery effects on their charms that <i>only</i> Dragon-Blooded can access, not even Solars or Sidereals. I debated having each Aspect only able to access the Mastery effects of their associated IMA, but she prefers Earth Dragon and that would bar her from them so I didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 07-30-2020, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T11:14:24-07:00","id":1405391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1405292#post1405292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope that the full write-up I provided has shown that you made some false assumptions of my intent.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> As for the bonus dice added, I have been operating under the impression that all bonuses added through the expenditure of essence are considered Charm bonuses by default (even when not provided by Charms)... so I have no idea how you got the impression that the bonuses would be considered non-Charm. Everything I have read points to this as the default assumption (though I do admit I may have overlooked or misread something). If I have, then it is an easy enough fix to state that the bonuses are considered Charm-based bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, you made a post listing your intent in which you said you wanted to preserve the 2E bonuses. I inferred from this that you wanted to port the artifact &quot;as is&quot;. When addressing your post, I was precise in my language (&quot;An always on, +1-5/+2-10 bonus in the style of the 2E artifact is hideodiously broken under the 3E paradigm&quot;). When addressing <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho\">GhanjRho </a></b>on their idea of a non-Charm bonus, I was imprecise in my language -- I apologise for any confusion caused.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1405292#post1405292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't trying to make Dragon-Blooded into the equivalent of Solars (in fact, I wasn't thinking of Dragon-Blooded at all when I started looking into this... I was actually aiming more towards Lunar Martial Artists to be honest). I also had every intent on doing this in such a way as to preserve Solar supremacy with Martial Arts by limiting just how much access one has to Mastery effects and under what conditions one can access such effects. The Solar position as the true Masters of the Martial Arts remains untouched... even if they aren't using this artifact and are fighting someone who is using it. I also wanted to create an artifact that even Solars and Sidereal would want to use, even if they don't need it to access Mastery effects. Finally, I wanted to make sure that the costs of using this artifact were equal to the benefits one gained by using it... something I felt that was not well thought out in your original version (very high costs and lots of hoops to jump through for a gain that didn't feel worth the price). True, my impression of your version of the bracers is a subjective one.... but one I feel is accurate (how many players in your games have asked for your version of the bracers... or how many of your own characters use it?).<br /> <br /> All that said, I am still not entirely sure I balanced my version well enough... especially with the second Evocation (feels a little... meh... to me). <b>I am curious as to your opinion now that you can more clearly see what I am aiming for with this artifact.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't hate it.<br /> <br /> A Lunar using my draft is committing 3m to attune then committing another 5m reflexively. A Lunar using yours is committing 8m. Obviously there's a difference in balance point (mine is harsher, yours is lower), but ultimately I think it's churlish of me to quibble. If this works for your game, then great.<br /> <br /> I have some questions, a couple of suggestions:<br /> <br /> I very much like how you've handled the powers of the artifact as Evocations. I think that really fits well with 3E.<br /> <br /> I really like the Solar effect of Blossoming of the Lotus. Charms have very specific balance points in their costs, and I was very hesitant about the idea of applying the 2E Starmetal discount, but you've handled it brilliantly. The game-breaking ultility of reducing a 5m Charm to 3m is offset by automatically flaring to Burning. The fact that the artifact has an 8m attunement means you have to use this four times to break-even. I think it's almost perfectly balanced. (I'm not sure why there's a one-turn grace period on your anima dropping -- I'd just have the Charm end if you hit Dim.)<br /> <br /> As stated previously, I don't think this should take you up more than a single level of Martial Arts (Terrestrial to Neutral, Neutral to Mastery), otherwise I think the non-Solar effect of Blossoming of the Lotus is fine. I think unlocking for free is also fine (you've put a higher attunement on your artifact than I did, and not offered any incidental benefits), but the player needs to know that this is going to flair their character's anima when they use a Form charm. Dragon-Blooded currently have to have peak mortal mastery of Martial Arts (5 dots) and be Immaculate Masters (five Charms) in order to ignore the Terrestrial keyword <i>for a single tick </i>when they expend Aura: I really don't feel that &quot;get indefinite Mastery with a free Evocation&quot; represents anything like a trade-off or alternative. It's not a cost -- it's a no-brainer. By contrast my idea (buy two Charms and commit your entire personal essence pool for Mastery) represents a real cost. Keep in mind also that Lunars, thanks to being able to use their Native Charms alongside Martial Arts are already as powerful as Solar Martial Artists (outside of Supernal, and non-Combat Charms/Evocations): whether that's going to cause balance problems is going to depend on your table. If we're taking this at character creation, then not so much (Lunar Charms and Martial Arts Charms come out of the same allowance), but if the Lunar has X sessions of Lunar Charms and Martial Arts Charms bought with LP, I can see there being some disparity.<br /> <br /> Making Perfected Kata Strike a Simple Charm sidesteps a lot of stacking problems. I'm hesitant about Charms that stack flat Decisive damage. Now understand, if a player is going to try and break Exalted, then they will succeed: there's no point trying to design an artifact that can't be abused. But the danger with Exalted is in breaking the game accidently. &quot;I want to be a shadowy assassin... I'll play a Dawn... Ebon Shadow Style looks perfect... I'll take a few Athletics Charms...&quot; You're now sitting on a Base Initiative of 7, and doubling your Decisive damage -- take this Artifact and you're adding 1-5 damage to that. Go out of your way to pick up a couple more entry level effects (Wind Rider Swiftness, Falling Scythe Flash) and you can make 20d Decisives with double damage from Base Initiative. There's some wording problems (you don't add Accuracy to Decisive attacks, but the intent is clear). I'd probably drop the Willpower cost and just have the Agg damage as a bene. I'd be tempted to make this a Dual Charm -- have the &quot;Accuracy&quot; bonus be uniform, shift the bonus damage to Withering damage (the bracers help you build up advantage against your foes), and have choosing your damage type (Bashing, Lethal or Aggravated against CoD) be the Decisive benefit.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think your artifact is too permissive. I wouldn't allow it &quot;as is&quot; in my game. But we're talking a matter of a few tweaks rather than a whole re-write -- I wouldn't force you to use my version instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1405292#post1405292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how many players in your games have asked for your version of the bracers... or how many of your own characters use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>None of my players are playing Martial Artists. And I made that version specifically for you because you asked for it in this thread.<br /> <br /> (My PC is a Dragon-Blooded martial artist, but I have no interest in acquiring Perfected Kata Bracers for him -- your version or mine.)<br /> <br /> It's fine that you think my version is over-costed. I hope I gave you some inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-30-2020, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T15:36:42-07:00","id":1405409,"title":"","content":"I do understand that my brainstorming of ideas was a little scattered and unrefined... which could easily lead to false impressions of intent. Brainstorming is kind of like that... I am just trying to figure out the effects I would like for the artifact, then once I know what I am after, then I figure out how to balance the effects so that the effort of getting it equals the benefit gained from it. Not sure how do describe this approach, but it works for me.<br /> <br /> Yes, I wasn't sure that going with Evocations was the right choice, but looking at the available artifacts so far, any that offer more than a single effect tend to present those effects as Evocations as opposed to innate effects.<br /> <br /> The Solar and Sidereal effect is designed to allow Exalts that have natural access to Mastery effects to still find some use from this artifact. Given the Anima flare that is produced when this effect is active, it made sense that they might be drawing on the natural Essence of the world to power their Charms... at least the ones that belong to the same Style as the Form they are in. It is a powerful effect, but with this limitation (plus the role-play opportunity of flare) I felt it was balance.<br /> <br /> As for why I allow the wielder a chance to flare their Anima after use is to allow them to maintain the effect without having to repay all the relevant costs. Remember, as stated in the evocation's description, not only is the Mastery effect lost, but the character is also forced out of their Form Charm (the commitment to the charm is released) when the effect ends. Most effects of this nature tend to allow a character the chance to re-establish the condition that maintains the effect before it is lost, so as not to be overly punishing to the player. To automatically end the effect without a chance to maintain it would tend to result in players not using charms with Anima costs as the Willpower cost (not to mention the significant mote cost of most Form Charms) is high (willpower doesn't regenerate during combat to the same degree that Essence motes do). Thus, I felt giving a character until the end of their next turn (which is consistent with a lot of charms that require conditions to maintain) was fair. There may not be many Martial Art charms that have anima costs, but they do exist and thus a player using that style should not feel like they need to avoid those charms of their chosen style to maintain this effect.<br /> <br /> Besides, just because they have the chance to flare their anima to maintain the effect doesn't mean they have to. This provides them with a choice, where not allowing them this chance takes away any choice. It is up to the player to decide whether or not to take the opportunities given to them.<br /> <br /> It is because of the Willpower cost that I am allowing this evocation to both nullify the applicability of the Terrestrial keyword and to allow access to the Mastery keyword. Unlike mere Motes, Willpower is a very finite resource for players and doesn't regenerate with each round of combat like Essence motes do. It is best described as the Martial Artist focusing a lot of their power into manifesting this effect... sort of like how many Anime fighters are powering up (even causing an anima flare effect too)... and should do more than what simple motes would accomplish. Given that to date only one type of Exalt is even affected by the Terrestrial keyword (though we can presume that weaker Exigents are likely subject to this limitation as well), I don't see what they need an extra hoop to jump through when thematically, it doesn't add much to the experience except make things a little harder for the player playing a slightly weaker character. The limitations of playing a character subject to the Terrestrial Keyword is already enough of a limitation, as they likely have smaller Essence pools to work with to begin with. I generally come at my designs from the perspective of what will be fun to play... not how to make something cool hard to attain just because of the player's choice of character splat.<br /> <br /> The trade off is when a character can use Mastery effects (only while in a Form Charm's effect) and which effects are applicable (only charms from the style they are in the Form of). For characters who only know a single Martial Art, this isn't a problem as they are only likely to use that style anyways. This is a limitation in and of itself... one that opponents could potentially exploit (and any Storyteller worth their salt will find ways to exploit the flaws of a single combat strategy should it make sense to do so). In short, the character that relies on a single style becomes predictable to a degree. Now for characters that learn multiple styles, this still limits their access to Mastery effects (well... at least for non-Solars and Sidereal) as they now need to choose which style has the Mastery effects they want to take advantage of. They are still free to mix and match Martial Art charms as they see fit, but will only benefit from the Mastery of a single style's charms at any given time. It really does come down to the player choosing how they wish to play... and the consequences of their choices. A player is more likely to accept the consequences of their own actions when they had the freedom to choose how they hang themselves as opposed to not having a choice in what happens. More hoops to jump through to get more evocations for relatively minor benefits (a lot of Mastery effects are not substantially powerful... significant yes, but not overly powerful)<br /> <br /> You don't add a Weapon's accuracy bonus to Decisive attacks... but you can still add dice through Charms to the accuracy of a Decisive Attack (all this means is adding dice to the attack roll). A Dex 5 Martial Arts 5 character is still rolling a base attack pool of 10, even if they are not getting the +3 accuracy bonus from their Reaper Daiklave... and can still increase this pool by Charms (or Excellencies). Perhaps rephrasing it to say that it adds to the attack roll rather than to accuracy would be a better choice of words. I did choose to make the evocation Simple to limit the amount of stacking possible... you got that part right... this is meant to represent the finishing move of a battle... a Kamehameha if you will. I fully expect players to try to make it as powerful as they can, as it is thematically appropriate to do so (though within normal limits as I will specify the added dice are considered to be Charm dice). I see this as a fun little option that I want players to take advantage of... thus I wanted it to be an attractive option among other attractive options they might have access to. Of course the player doesn't manage to finish the fight with this attack (or any other attack they might try), then I will do my best to go full Freeza on their ass should the opportunity arise (and from time to time it has).<br /> <br /> As for the ability to combine other charms with Martial Arts, even Lunars do have a degree of limitations in this respect (not as much as Ability based Exalts mind you). That these additional charms will not benefit from the Bracers and will tax the Lunar's resources for combat (motes, willpower, initiative, anima) will place limitations of what they can achieve even with access of Mastery. Of course they can blow all their motes, willpower, imitative and even anima into a single powerful attack (any Exalt an do so in theory), but the consequences of doing so should be obvious. Any player who does that quickly learns that it may look cool, but often costs them the battle as they put too much power into a single effort when they should have been pacing themselves. Combat is a marathon where one needs to dole out their power over the long run rather than spend it all at once as if it were a sprint or a dash. I am not worried about players trying to make one powerful attack because only the inexperienced and foolish make that mistake more than once (and I take full advantage of such mistakes when players make them, to show them why such tactics are not the best course of action). I think this is one case where we are coming at things from two very different perspectives... you seem afraid that players might abuse an effect and try to make it so the effect can't be abused. I however approach things from the perspective that players will find a way to abuse any mechanic, thus I let them show me their exploit and then show them why it may not be the advantage they think it is... I let them be the powerful demi-gods they are and let the consequences of often ill thought out plans show them their error rather than try (and likely fail) to reign in their power. Yes, there are times when they actually found an exploit that is both powerful and has few drawbacks or consequences for me to exploit in return... but if those turn out to be fun for everyone (I love it when players discover something I overlooked, even if it is often frustrating) we may keep it open. If it becomes a problem we work together to deal with it... sort of what you and I are doing now... so that it is something everyone can enjoy without anyone feeling like they are being punished for their creativity.<br /> <br /> To be honest though, your version of the Bracers was definitely inspirational... I saw what you were going for... and how costly it would be for characters using it. I may not agree with that approach, but it did help me refine the concept I was going for. You probably don't agree with a lot of my reasoning for the costs and benefits I put into my version of the Bracers... which is fine (to be honest I am not sure my reasoning is entirely sound at times), but that is what I like about these forums... most people can respectfully disagree and discuss their perspectives and hopefully come to an agreement... even if it just to agree to disagree. I think your example has been the most help I got as it actually provided me what I needed to know, even if I didn't agree with the direction you took. Different people will approach the same problem from different angles... and that can give a person insight they may not have considered from their own perspective. That was definitely the case here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T16:06:21-07:00","id":1405412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404465-mastery-through-artifice?p=1405409#post1405409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is because of the Willpower cost that I am allowing this evocation to both nullify the applicability of the Terrestrial keyword and to allow access to the Mastery keyword. Unlike mere Motes, Willpower is a very finite resource for players and doesn't regenerate with each round of combat like Essence motes do. It is best described as the Martial Artist focusing a lot of their power into manifesting this effect... sort of like how many Anime fighters are powering up (even causing an anima flare effect too)... and should do more than what simple motes would accomplish. Given that to date only one type of Exalt is even affected by the Terrestrial keyword (though we can presume that weaker Exigents are likely subject to this limitation as well), I don't see what they need an extra hoop to jump through when thematically, it doesn't add much to the experience except make things a little harder for the player playing a slightly weaker character. The limitations of playing a character subject to the Terrestrial Keyword is already enough of a limitation, as they likely have smaller Essence pools to work with to begin with. I generally come at my designs from the perspective of what will be fun to play... not how to make something cool hard to attain just because of the player's choice of character splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your reasoning for taking DBs straight to Mastery is that you feel the Terrestrial keyword is not a fun mechanic period (a thought I definitely agree with), then I'd suggest fixing that separately from the Bracers. You could simply houserule away the Terrestrial keyword in your games (possibly adjusting immaculate styles to add Mastery for 1 tick instead of removing Terrestrial). That way the Bracer will offer the same level of powering up to DBs as it does to Lunars/Sids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}